# Do NOT let Git rewrite line endings.
#
# sync.ps1 compares the deployed skill against the source with SHA256. Any checkout-time
# line-ending conversion (text=auto, eol=crlf, ...) would make every file look "different"
# after a fresh clone, turning a real integrity check into a false alarm.
#
# Files are stored byte-for-byte as written. The .ps1 scripts are ASCII-only by convention,
# and PowerShell 5.1 parses LF fine, so no normalization is needed.
* -text
